 345:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @brief  Find last matching subsequence in a sequence.
 346:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @ingroup non_mutating_algorithms
 347:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @param  __first1  Start of range to search.
 348:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @param  __last1   End of range to search.
 349:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @param  __first2  Start of sequence to match.
 350:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @param  __last2   End of sequence to match.
 351:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @return   The last iterator @c i in the range
 352:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @p [__first1,__last1-(__last2-__first2)) such that @c *(i+N) ==
 353:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  @p *(__first2+N) for each @c N in the range @p
 354:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  [0,__last2-__first2), or @p __last1 if no such iterator exists.
 355:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *
 356:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  Searches the range @p [__first1,__last1) for a sub-sequence that
 357:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  compares equal value-by-value with the sequence given by @p
 358:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  [__first2,__last2) and returns an iterator to the __first
 359:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  element of the sub-sequence, or @p __last1 if the sub-sequence
 360:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  is not found.  The sub-sequence will be the last such
 361:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  subsequence contained in [__first1,__last1).
 362:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *
 363:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  Because the sub-sequence must lie completely within the range @p
 364:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  [__first1,__last1) it must start at a position less than @p
 365:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  __last1-(__last2-__first2) where @p __last2-__first2 is the
 366:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  length of the sub-sequence.  This means that the returned
 367:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_algo.h ****    *  iterator @c i will be in the range @p
